      "body": "This partitions the oversized daemon, runtime, Codex adapter, Protect, encrypted store, supply-chain, CLI/test and dashboard families around the Rust runtime integration. Reviewed partitions fit within 500 physical lines per file. Ordered definitions, live facade lookups, descriptors, captured defaults and package anchors remain source-verified; policy/approval authority, receipt persistence and cleanup boundaries retain their existing contracts. The CI repairs cover corpus ranking/process coordination, heredocs, source-location assertions and synthetic fixtures; independently resolved wheels require `anyio>=4.14.2`.\n\nReviewed integration checkpoint: [`99f2b78f`](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/commit/99f2b78f173d10f2b1d60da2a58da65663a83311), tree `a10d23795cb689f9ca4dd43fcc82d5f769847a99`, sole parent `a37a5df6`. It preserves the incoming navigation change: the contract reads `app-routing.ts` and checks the real `app.tsx` import. The combined source contains the actual generated corpus report.\n\n| Source-bound validation | Actual result |\n| --- | --- |\n| [Four partitions](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/actions/runs/35439228147) and [Codex follow-up](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/actions/runs/35440934952) | Protect 32, command 75, Surface 114 passed/one declared Darwin skip; Codex 21 existing cases plus nine separate controls passed. Paired collection, source, package and default secret-scan evidence remains separately bound. |\n| [StoreBase](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/actions/runs/35442131469) and [LSC installed follow-up](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/actions/runs/35444566127) | Store: 36 passed; scoped Ruff, types and source gates passed. LSC: 613 existing plus 25 source controls passed; a fresh 25 installed-wheel controls passed with package/dependency identity unchanged. |\n| [Package evaluator](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/actions/runs/35448416289) | 12 unchanged controls and three route cases passed; the 17 earlier passing cases retain exact current collection/fixture/source bindings without body replay. All 21 type targets passed. |\n| [Final immutable corpus](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/actions/runs/35449285579) | 51,000 cases, all 452 input bindings, report check and six original contracts passed. Both measured runs stayed below the unchanged 60 s/512 MiB limits: 57.272/56.952 s and 314.098/315.414 MiB. |\n| [Original main CI evidence](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/actions/runs/35433592816) | All 718 runtime cases are now attributable as passed from the exact plan, call records and complete original file-progress logs. That original overall CI run remains failed; its unrelated failures are preserved. |\n\nThese are component and corpus results, not a green final-head CI claim. Earlier failures remain linked in the [durable handoff](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/tree/75bb8692b5eaaf6f2e138d5da20402b7d270a9bb/review-evidence/2026-09-19/pr2974-completion), including the package metric failure, temporary-root failures and observer corrections. The [15:09 UTC evidence addendum](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/blob/7337ab5400eebfe5634e43f32122f3be6500b7cd/review-evidence/2026-09-19/pr2974-completion/addenda/2026-09-19T150913Z/README.md) preserves the subsequent component results, cancelled workflows, Intel latency failures and CodeQL finding. Later source commits require their own applicable validation. Existing behavioral assertions and budgets were preserved. No ignored-secret rules were added; the existing 152-entry ignore file remains unchanged.\n\nThe [original PRD, TODO and Takeaway](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/tree/75bb8692b5eaaf6f2e138d5da20402b7d270a9bb/review-evidence/2026-09-19/pr2974-completion/originals) and [144-item current worklist](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/blob/75bb8692b5eaaf6f2e138d5da20402b7d270a9bb/review-evidence/2026-09-19/pr2974-completion/TODO-current.md) preserve the acceptance contract and all 144 original task objects/119 catalog entries: 74 claimed DONE, 31 OPEN, 29 BLOCKED, ten DEFERRED. The 74 claimed DONE items retain unresolved acceptance dependencies; no tasks are promoted.\n\nRelease acceptance remains open: final-head full CI, combined package/installed controls, the actual release-range secret scan, applicable review findings, OCI trust-boundary/upstream decisions, fresh Greptile 5/5 and genuine independent last-push/CODEOWNER approval. Installed p95/p99 50/100 ms, c16 p99 200 ms, readiness 400 ms, original sampling, 30% benefit/5% regression limits, SQLite/process-tree attribution, workspace 1/10/100, resource/soak, rollback, signing and canary requirements are unchanged. RSP-100's four correctness witnesses passed while its unsafe optimization stays off. Native phase, SQLite/queue and installed qualification work continues separately. The [next work and owners](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/blob/75bb8692b5eaaf6f2e138d5da20402b7d270a9bb/review-evidence/2026-09-19/pr2974-completion/NEXT-IMPLEMENTATION.md) distinguish code, measured deferrals and external blockers.\n",
